:false,"open_issues_count":2143,"license":{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["data-analysis","data-science","machine-learning","python","statistics"],"visibility":"public","forks":26756,"open_issues":2143,"watchers":65403,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/pulls/2426","html_url":"https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/pull/2426","diff_url":"https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/pull/2426.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/pull/2426.patch","merged_at":"2013-09-21T15:39:07Z"},"body":"Here are some safe bits from #2419, which can be pulled without waiting for my threading experiments.\n- nogil declarations where possible (but no with nogil blocks, since the performance benefit of those is not clear)\n- use BLAS where appropriate\n- replaced DOUBLE by double, INTEGER and int32 by int/np.intc, since that's the type used by scipy.sparse\n- explicit checks that dataset dims don't exceed INT_MAX\n- replaced an np.all by an explicit loop (npymath library for C99 isfinite)\n\nI also cleaned up the code a little bit (e.g. `min` and `max` no longer need to be defined for current Cython).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/2426/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/2426/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/comments/24027426","html_url":"https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/2393#issuecomment-24027426","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/2393","id":24027426,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0MDI3NDI2","user":{"login":"larsmans","id":335383,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNTM4Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/335383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans","html_url":"https://github.com/larsmans","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larsmans/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-09-08T19:23:50Z","updated_at":"2013-09-08T19:23:50Z","body":"I think this is not a bug in scikit-learn but either a bug in NumPy or one of those stange memory management \"features\" in the Linux kernel:\n\n```\n>>> data = np.memmap('/dev/shm/features.dat', dtype='float64', mode='w+', shape=(40000000,100))\n>>> data[:] += 1\nBus error\n```\n\nImmediately after, my browser was killed. Disabling the OOM killer did not change this.\n\nI've seen similar strangeness with `np.memmap` on Linux about a week ago, when I managed to bring a compute server to its knees by mapping and filling 10 files each just 10MB large. I don't think we can do anything about this, so I'm closing the issue.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.